  "source": {
    "source_id": "companion-domain:pbps-actual-hazard-clock",
    "anchor": "arXiv2609.06905v1 Algorithm1, Proposition3.1, AppendixA.1 equation(A.1), Ex1-8; one-segment prerequisites for recursive equation(A.2).",
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A1",
    "original_text": "Fan Chen, Sinho Chewi, Jianfeng Lu and Matthew S. Zhang, arXiv:2609.06905v1, Algorithm1 and AppendixA.1 equation(A.1), Ex1–8. ASTIS supplies omitted continuous-first-crossing and measure details. Recursive equation(A.2) and the full Proposition3.1 stochastic construction remain later consumers.\nLet E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space, including rank zero. Let V:E→ℝ be C², let α,β≥0 satisfy 0<α≤β and α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for all x,v, and let η>0 with βη≤1. For arbitrary y,xRef and z=(x,p), define c=y−η∇V(xRef), Φ_t(z)=(c+cos(t)(x−c)+√η sin(t)p, −sin(t)(x−c)/√η+cos(t)p), λ(xRef,(u,q))=√η max(0,⟨q,∇V(u)−∇V(xRef)⟩), H(z)=(η⁻¹‖x−c‖²+‖p‖²)/2, and C(z)=√η β√(2H(z))(√(2ηH(z))+‖c−xRef‖). For t≥0 put Λ_z(t)=∫₀ᵗλ(xRef,Φ_s(z))ds and τ_z(e)=inf{t≥0:Λ_z(t)≥e}, returning ∞ when this set is empty. Let W_z be the pushforward of Exp(1) on ℝ by e↦τ_z(max(e,0)). Then: (1) Λ is jointly continuous in y,xRef,z,t; (2) Λ is jointly Borel; (3) the actual orbit rate is integrable on every finite [0,t]; (4) Λ_z(0)=0, Λ_z(t)≥0 and Λ_z is nondecreasing; (5) for every e,t≥0, τ_z(e)≤t iff e≤Λ_z(t); (6) τ_z(e)=∞ iff Λ_z(t)<e for every finite t, finite τ_z(e) satisfies Λ_z(τ_z(e))=e, e>0 implies τ_z(e)>0, and τ_z(0)=0; (7) τ is jointly Borel in y,xRef,z,e; (8) W_z is a probability measure on [0,∞] and W_z((t,∞])=exp(−Λ_z(t)) for every finite t; (9) C(z)≥0 and Λ_z(t)≤C(z)t; (10) C(z)>0 implies max(e/C(z),0)≤τ_z(e), while C(z)=0 and e>0 imply τ_z(e)=∞. Every conclusion is derived for the actual flow and rate using their compiled laws. No unbounded-hazard or almost-sure finite-wait assumption is made. This is one flow-segment clock law used by AppendixA.1(A.1) and the future recursion(A.2). Recursive paths, nonexplosion, Markov memorylessness, invariance, terminal sampling kernels, main bounds and query costs remain open.\narXiv2609.06905v1 Algorithm1, Proposition3.1, AppendixA.1 equation(A.1), Ex1-8; one-segment prerequisites for recursive equation(A.2).",
    "text_sha256": "db14e7122122eefa82f5ccfc467bfed011011f415a8318aaeb72fa3b7f54c19e"
  },
  "lean": {
    "statement": "\n    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {V : E → ℝ} {α β : ℝ≥0} {η : ℝ}\n    (hα : 0 < (α : ℝ)) (hαβ : α ≤ β) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E,\n      (α : ℝ) * ‖v‖ ^ 2 ≤ (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ∧\n      (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ≤ (β : ℝ) * ‖v‖ ^ 2)\n    (hη : 0 < η) (hβη : (β : ℝ) * η ≤ 1) :\n    let c : E → E → E := fun y xRef => y - η • gradient V xRef\n    let Φ : E → E → ℝ → (E × E) → (E × E) := fun y xRef t z =>\n      (c y xRef + Real.cos t • (z.1 - c y xRef) +\n          (Real.sqrt η * Real.sin t) • z.2,\n       (-Real.sin t / Real.sqrt η) • (z.1 - c y xRef) + Real.cos t • z.2)\n    let rate : E → (E × E) → ℝ := fun xRef z =>\n      Real.sqrt η * max 0 (inner ℝ z.2 (gradient V z.1 - gradient V xRef))\n    let H : E → E → (E × E) → ℝ := fun y xRef z =>\n      (η⁻¹ * ‖z.1 - c y xRef‖ ^ 2 + ‖z.2‖ ^ 2) / 2\n    let C : E → E → (E × E) → ℝ := fun y xRef z =>\n      Real.sqrt η * (β : ℝ) * Real.sqrt (2 * H y xRef z) *\n        (Real.sqrt (2 * η * H y xRef z) + ‖c y xRef - xRef‖)\n    let Λ : E → E → (E × E) → ℝ≥0 → ℝ := fun y xRef z t =>\n      ∫ s in (0 : ℝ)..(t : ℝ), rate xRef (Φ y xRef s z)\n    let τ : E → E → (E × E) → ℝ≥0 → WithTop ℝ≥0 := fun y xRef z e =>\n      MeasureTheory.hittingAfter\n        (fun t : ℝ≥0 => fun a : (E × E) × (E × E) × ℝ≥0 =>\n          Λ a.1.1 a.1.2 a.2.1 t - (a.2.2 : ℝ))\n        (Set.Ici (0 : ℝ)) 0 ((y, xRef), z, e)\n    let W : E → E → (E × E) → Measure (WithTop ℝ≥0) := fun y xRef z =>\n      Measure.map (fun e : ℝ => τ y xRef z (Real.toNNReal e))\n        (ProbabilityTheory.expMeasure (1 : ℝ))\n    Continuous (fun a : ((E × E) × (E × E)) × ℝ≥0 =>\n      Λ a.1.1.1 a.1.1.2 a.1.2 a.2) ∧\n    Measurable (fun a : ((E × E) × (E × E)) × ℝ≥0 =>\n      Λ a.1.1.1 a.1.1.2 a.1.2 a.2) ∧\n    (∀ y xRef : E, ∀ z : E × E, ∀ t : ℝ≥0,\n      IntervalIntegrable (fun s : ℝ => rate xRef (Φ y xRef s z)) volume 0 (t : ℝ)) ∧\n    (∀ y xRef : E, ∀ z : E × E,\n      Λ y xRef z 0 = 0 ∧ (∀ t : ℝ≥0, 0 ≤ Λ y xRef z t) ∧\n      Monotone (Λ y xRef z)) ∧\n    (∀ y xRef : E, ∀ z : E × E, ∀ e t : ℝ≥0,\n      τ y xRef z e ≤ (t : WithTop ℝ≥0) ↔ (e : ℝ) ≤ Λ y xRef z t) ∧\n    (∀ y xRef : E, ∀ z : E × E, ∀ e : ℝ≥0,\n      (τ y xRef z e = ⊤ ↔ ∀ t : ℝ≥0, Λ y xRef z t < (e : ℝ)) ∧\n      (τ y xRef z e ≠ ⊤ → Λ y xRef z (τ y xRef z e).untopA = (e : ℝ)) ∧\n      (0 < e → (0 : WithTop ℝ≥0) < τ y xRef z e) ∧ τ y xRef z 0 = 0) ∧\n    Measurable (fun a : (E × E) × (E × E) × ℝ≥0 =>\n      τ a.1.1 a.1.2 a.2.1 a.2.2) ∧\n    (∀ y xRef : E, ∀ z : E × E, IsProbabilityMeasure (W y xRef z) ∧\n      ∀ t : ℝ≥0, (W y xRef z).real (Set.Ioi (t : WithTop ℝ≥0)) =\n        Real.exp (-Λ y xRef z t)) ∧\n    (∀ y xRef : E, ∀ z : E × E, 0 ≤ C y xRef z ∧\n      ∀ t : ℝ≥0, Λ y xRef z t ≤ C y xRef z * (t : ℝ)) ∧\n    (∀ y xRef : E, ∀ z : E × E, ∀ e : ℝ≥0,\n      (0 < C y xRef z →\n        (Real.toNNReal ((e : ℝ) / C y xRef z) : WithTop ℝ≥0) ≤ τ y xRef z e) ∧\n      (C y xRef z = 0 → 0 < e → τ y xRef z e = ⊤))",
    "statement_sha256": "dbfec4ed1bb16f05fab2946634233819f8a41b85bdc6da816e25a8b21fb5d3f1",
    "compiled": true,
    "decoder_context": [
      "The ambient space is finite-dimensional over the reals with its compatible norm and real inner product. Its measurable structure is Borel; products use product topology and measurable structure. Rank zero is allowed.",
      "gradient is the Hilbert gradient represented by the Frechet derivative. The displayed iterated Frechet derivative applied twice to v is the Hessian quadratic form. ContDiff order 2 means twice continuously Frechet differentiable.",
      "All eight displayed let definitions are literal. H is the weighted sum of two separate squared vector norms; C uses that same initial state energy. Real division is total and Real.sqrt is the nonnegative real square root.",
      "NNReal is the set of nonnegative reals. WithTop NNReal adjoins a largest element infinity. The untopA operation extracts its finite value and has a default value at infinity; the finite-value equality has an explicit non-infinity guard.",
      "hittingAfter is the infimum of the times at or after its given start whose process value is in the given target set. It returns infinity when that set is empty. Time here is continuous NNReal, not a well-founded discrete order.",
      "The notation integral s in 0..t is the oriented real interval integral with respect to real Lebesgue measure. IntervalIntegrable is integrability on the interval in both orientations.",
      "expMeasure(1) is the real exponential probability measure of rate one, supported on nonnegative reals. Real.toNNReal sends a real number to its nonnegative part. Measure.map is pushforward along the displayed first-time function.",
      "Measure.real(A) is the real value of the measure of A. IsProbabilityMeasure explicitly asserts total mass one. Ioi(t) is the strict upper interval, including infinity in the extended time space."
    ],
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.ActualHazardClock.actual_integrated_hazard_clock_laws",
