      ],
      "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space, including rank zero. Let V:E→ℝ be C², let α,β≥0 satisfy 0<α≤β and α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for all x,v, and let η>0 with βη≤1. For arbitrary y,xRef and z=(x,p), define c=y−η∇V(xRef), Φ_t(z)=(c+cos(t)(x−c)+√η sin(t)p, −sin(t)(x−c)/√η+cos(t)p), λ(xRef,(u,q))=√η max(0,⟨q,∇V(u)−∇V(xRef)⟩), H(z)=(η⁻¹‖x−c‖²+‖p‖²)/2, and C(z)=√η β√(2H(z))(√(2ηH(z))+‖c−xRef‖). For t≥0 put Λ_z(t)=∫₀ᵗλ(xRef,Φ_s(z))ds and τ_z(e)=inf{t≥0:Λ_z(t)≥e}, returning ∞ when this set is empty. Let W_z be the pushforward of Exp(1) on ℝ by e↦τ_z(max(e,0)). Then: (1) Λ is jointly continuous in y,xRef,z,t; (2) Λ is jointly Borel; (3) the actual orbit rate is integrable on every finite [0,t]; (4) Λ_z(0)=0, Λ_z(t)≥0 and Λ_z is nondecreasing; (5) for every e,t≥0, τ_z(e)≤t iff e≤Λ_z(t); (6) τ_z(e)=∞ iff Λ_z(t)<e for every finite t, finite τ_z(e) satisfies Λ_z(τ_z(e))=e, e>0 implies τ_z(e)>0, and τ_z(0)=0; (7) τ is jointly Borel in y,xRef,z,e; (8) W_z is a probability measure on [0,∞] and W_z((t,∞])=exp(−Λ_z(t)) for every finite t; (9) C(z)≥0 and Λ_z(t)≤C(z)t; (10) C(z)>0 implies max(e/C(z),0)≤τ_z(e), while C(z)=0 and e>0 imply τ_z(e)=∞. Every conclusion is derived for the actual flow and rate using their compiled laws. No unbounded-hazard or almost-sure finite-wait assumption is made. This is one flow-segment clock law used by AppendixA.1(A.1) and the future recursion(A.2). Recursive paths, nonexplosion, Markov memorylessness, invariance, terminal sampling kernels, main bounds and query costs remain open.",
      "formula": "c=y-\\eta\\nabla V(x_{\\rm ref}),\\quad\\Phi_t(x,p)=\\bigl(c+\\cos t(x-c)+\\sqrt\\eta\\sin t\\,p,-\\tfrac{\\sin t}{\\sqrt\\eta}(x-c)+\\cos t\\,p\\bigr).\\quad \\lambda(x_{\\rm ref},(x,p))=\\sqrt\\eta\\max\\{0,\\langle p,\\nabla V(x)-\\nabla V(x_{\\rm ref})\\rangle\\},\\quad H(z)=\\tfrac12(\\eta^{-1}\\|x-c\\|^2+\\|p\\|^2),\\quad C(z)=\\sqrt\\eta\\,\\beta\\sqrt{2H(z)}\\bigl(\\sqrt{2\\eta H(z)}+\\|c-x_{\\rm ref}\\|\\bigr).\\quad \\Lambda_z(t)=\\int_0^t\\lambda(x_{\\rm ref},\\Phi_s z)\\,ds,\\quad\\tau_z(e)=\\inf\\{t\\ge0:\\Lambda_z(t)\\ge e\\}\\in[0,\\infty],\\quad\\inf\\varnothing=\\infty.\\quad W_z=(e\\mapsto\\tau_z(\\max\\{e,0\\}))_\\#\\operatorname{Exp}(1),\\quad W_z((t,\\infty])=e^{-\\Lambda_z(t)},\\quad\\Lambda_z(t)\\le C(z)t,\\quad\\tau_z(e)\\ge e/C(z)\\ (C(z)>0).",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Reuse the actual flow, rate and conserved-energy bound",
          "text": "Take joint flow continuity and exact H conservation from the compiled harmonic-flow theorem, and rate continuity/nonnegativity and the same-energy-layer bound from the compiled bounce/rate theorem. Substitute Φ_s(z) into that bound and use H(Φ_s(z))=H(z). Positivity of the displayed factors proves C(z)≥0.",
          "formula": "\\lambda(x_{\\rm ref},\\Phi_s z)\\ge0,\\quad H(\\Phi_s z)=H(z),\\quad\\lambda(x_{\\rm ref},\\Phi_s z)\\le C(z),\\quad C(z)\\ge0.",
          "lean": "  have hf := ActualHarmonicFlow.actual_harmonic_flow_laws hα hαβ hV hH hη hβη\n  have hb := ActualBounceRate.actual_bounce_rate_energy_laws hα hαβ hV hH hη hβη\n  have hΦ : Continuous (fun a : (E × E) × ℝ × (E × E) =>\n      Φ a.1.1 a.1.2 a.2.1 a.2.2) := hf.1\n  have hrate : Continuous (fun a : E × (E × E) => rate a.1 a.2) := hb.2.1\n  have hrate0 (xRef : E) (z : E × E) : 0 ≤ rate xRef z :=\n    (hb.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.1 xRef z).1\n  have henergy (y xRef : E) (s : ℝ) (z : E × E) :\n      H y xRef (Φ y xRef s z) = H y xRef z := hf.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.1 y xRef s z\n  have hcap (y xRef : E) (z : E × E) (s : ℝ) :\n      rate xRef (Φ y xRef s z) ≤ C y xRef z :=\n    (hb.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2 y xRef z).2 (Φ y xRef s z) (henergy y xRef s z) |>.2.2\n  have hC (y xRef : E) (z : E × E) : 0 ≤ C y xRef z := by\n    dsimp [C]\n    positivity\n",
          "detail": "Exact contiguous compiled BODY; the literal local definitions and preceding facts remain in scope. The first three blocks are the internal primitive helper, then the public first-clock proof.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/ActualHazardClock.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "fd93d01583eec206285573c1f1631b94739f95471c50e1ff940e66080238e23d",
            "start_line": 136,
            "end_line": 150,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "ec95c1c1f01285f6b458e92dcaaeb249272892001fc4f4dce80deac342c81af5"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Construct the continuous cumulative hazard",
          "text": "The actual joint orbit rate is continuous. The parameter-dependent primitive theorem with real Lebesgue measure gives joint continuity of its integral up to t; restricting the endpoint to NNReal preserves continuity and Borel measurability. For each fixed phase, direct trigonometric continuity of Φ and continuity of λ prove interval integrability on every finite real interval.",
          "formula": "(y,x_{\\rm ref},z,t)\\longmapsto\\Lambda_z(t)\\text{ is continuous and Borel},\\qquad\\lambda(x_{\\rm ref},\\Phi_\\cdot z)\\in L^1([0,t]).",
          "lean": "  have hF : Continuous (fun a : ((E × E) × (E × E)) × ℝ =>\n      rate a.1.1.2 (Φ a.1.1.1 a.1.1.2 a.2 a.1.2)) := by\n    exact hrate.comp (continuous_fst.fst.snd.prodMk\n      (hΦ.comp ((continuous_fst.fst).prodMk\n        (continuous_snd.prodMk continuous_fst.snd))))\n  have hΛ : Continuous (fun a : ((E × E) × (E × E)) × ℝ≥0 =>\n      Λ a.1.1.1 a.1.1.2 a.1.2 a.2) := by\n    exact (intervalIntegral.continuous_parametric_primitive_of_continuous\n      (f := fun (q : (E × E) × (E × E)) (s : ℝ) =>\n        rate q.1.2 (Φ q.1.1 q.1.2 s q.2)) (μ := volume) (a₀ := 0) hF).comp\n      (continuous_fst.prodMk (NNReal.continuous_coe.comp continuous_snd))\n  have hInt (y xRef : E) (z : E × E) (a b : ℝ) :\n      IntervalIntegrable (fun s : ℝ => rate xRef (Φ y xRef s z)) volume a b := by\n    have hsΦ : Continuous (fun s : ℝ => Φ y xRef s z) := by\n      dsimp [Φ]\n      fun_prop\n    have hc : Continuous (fun s : ℝ => rate xRef (Φ y xRef s z)) :=\n      hrate.comp (continuous_const.prodMk hsΦ)\n    exact hc.intervalIntegrable a b\n",
          "detail": "Exact contiguous compiled BODY; the literal local definitions and preceding facts remain in scope. The first three blocks are the internal primitive helper, then the public first-clock proof.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/ActualHazardClock.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "fd93d01583eec206285573c1f1631b94739f95471c50e1ff940e66080238e23d",
            "start_line": 151,
            "end_line": 169,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "f711ef1b6e91ecb2242995d1060268092a5eab081d526b5d847ae84e086fc9f2"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Derive monotonicity and the integrated cap",
          "text": "The empty interval gives Λ(0)=0. Nonnegativity of the actual integrand gives Λ(t)≥0. Integral monotonicity on nested nonnegative intervals gives Λ(s)≤Λ(t) when s≤t. Integrating the same actual pointwise bound C(z) gives Λ(t)≤C(z)t. Collect these facts in the private helper; no integral or cap certificate becomes a public caller.",
          "formula": "\\Lambda_z(0)=0,\\quad0\\le\\Lambda_z(s)\\le\\Lambda_z(t)\\le C(z)t\\quad(0\\le s\\le t).",
          "lean": "  have hbasic (y xRef : E) (z : E × E) :\n      Λ y xRef z 0 = 0 ∧ (∀ t : ℝ≥0, 0 ≤ Λ y xRef z t) ∧\n      Monotone (Λ y xRef z) := by\n    refine ⟨by simp [Λ], ?_, ?_⟩\n    · intro t\n      exact intervalIntegral.integral_nonneg_of_forall t.coe_nonneg\n        (fun s => hrate0 xRef (Φ y xRef s z))\n    · intro s t hst\n      exact intervalIntegral.integral_mono_interval (le_refl 0) s.coe_nonneg\n        (show (s : ℝ) ≤ t from hst)\n        (Filter.Eventually.of_forall (fun u => hrate0 xRef (Φ y xRef u z)))\n        (hInt y xRef z 0 t)\n  have hbound (y xRef : E) (z : E × E) (t : ℝ≥0) :\n      Λ y xRef z t ≤ C y xRef z * (t : ℝ) := by\n    have hi := intervalIntegral.integral_mono_on t.coe_nonneg\n      (hInt y xRef z 0 t) (intervalIntegrable_const (μ := volume))\n      (fun s _ => hcap y xRef z s)\n    simpa only [intervalIntegral.integral_const, sub_zero, smul_eq_mul, mul_comm] using hi\n  exact ⟨hΛ, hΛ.measurable, fun y xRef z t => hInt y xRef z 0 t,\n    hbasic, fun y xRef z => ⟨hC y xRef z, hbound y xRef z⟩⟩\n",
          "detail": "Exact contiguous compiled BODY; the literal local definitions and preceding facts remain in scope. The first three blocks are the internal primitive helper, then the public first-clock proof.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/ActualHazardClock.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "fd93d01583eec206285573c1f1631b94739f95471c50e1ff940e66080238e23d",
            "start_line": 170,
            "end_line": 189,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "8e97a942af840677ef6f7d2a3389b785cc59ec572a1c07c3a24b33c92736432a"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Identify the exact finite-time crossing event",
          "text": "Reuse the proved primitive facts with their folded local types. The set A_e={s≥0:e≤Λ(s)} is closed by continuity. If A_e is nonempty, its infimum belongs to A_e because it is bounded below; monotonicity gives inf A_e≤t iff e≤Λ(t). If it is empty, τ=∞ and both sides are false. This is a closed-set argument on continuous NNReal time.",
          "formula": "\\tau_z(e)\\le t\\iff e\\le\\Lambda_z(t),\\qquad\\tau_z(e)=\\infty\\iff\\forall t\\ge0,\\ \\Lambda_z(t)<e.",
          "lean": "  classical\n  have hp :\n      Continuous (fun a : ((E × E) × (E × E)) × ℝ≥0 =>\n        Λ a.1.1.1 a.1.1.2 a.1.2 a.2) ∧\n      Measurable (fun a : ((E × E) × (E × E)) × ℝ≥0 =>\n        Λ a.1.1.1 a.1.1.2 a.1.2 a.2) ∧\n      (∀ y xRef : E, ∀ z : E × E, ∀ t : ℝ≥0,\n        IntervalIntegrable (fun s : ℝ => rate xRef (Φ y xRef s z)) volume 0 (t : ℝ)) ∧\n      (∀ y xRef : E, ∀ z : E × E,\n        Λ y xRef z 0 = 0 ∧ (∀ t : ℝ≥0, 0 ≤ Λ y xRef z t) ∧\n        Monotone (Λ y xRef z)) ∧\n      (∀ y xRef : E, ∀ z : E × E, 0 ≤ C y xRef z ∧\n        ∀ t : ℝ≥0, Λ y xRef z t ≤ C y xRef z * (t : ℝ)) :=\n    actual_hazard_primitive_laws hα hαβ hV hH hη hβη\n  rcases hp with ⟨hΛ, hΛmeas, hInt, hbasic, hcaps⟩\n  have hcont (y xRef : E) (z : E × E) : Continuous (Λ y xRef z) :=\n    hΛ.comp (show Continuous (fun t : ℝ≥0 => (((y, xRef), z), t)) from\n      continuous_const.prodMk continuous_id)\n  have hτle (y xRef : E) (z : E × E) (e t : ℝ≥0) :\n      τ y xRef z e ≤ (t : WithTop ℝ≥0) ↔ (e : ℝ) ≤ Λ y xRef z t := by\n    dsimp only [τ, MeasureTheory.hittingAfter]\n    simp only [Set.mem_Ici, sub_nonneg, zero_le, true_and]\n    split_ifs with hex\n    · simp only [WithTop.coe_le_coe]\n      constructor\n      · intro h\n        have hc : IsClosed {s : ℝ≥0 | (e : ℝ) ≤ Λ y xRef z s} :=\n          isClosed_le continuous_const (hcont y xRef z)\n        exact (hc.csInf_mem hex (OrderBot.bddBelow _)).trans\n          ((hbasic y xRef z).2.2 h)\n      · intro he\n        exact csInf_le (OrderBot.bddBelow _) he\n    · constructor\n      · intro h\n        exact False.elim (WithTop.not_top_le_coe t h)\n      · intro he\n        exact False.elim (hex ⟨t, he⟩)\n  have hτtop (y xRef : E) (z : E × E) (e : ℝ≥0) :\n      τ y xRef z e = ⊤ ↔ ∀ t : ℝ≥0, Λ y xRef z t < (e : ℝ) := by\n    simp only [τ, MeasureTheory.hittingAfter_eq_top_iff, Set.mem_Ici,\n      sub_nonneg, zero_le, true_implies, not_le]\n",
          "detail": "Exact contiguous compiled BODY; the literal local definitions and preceding facts remain in scope. The first three blocks are the internal primitive helper, then the public first-clock proof.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/ActualHazardClock.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "fd93d01583eec206285573c1f1631b94739f95471c50e1ff940e66080238e23d",
            "start_line": 251,
            "end_line": 291,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "6a65cf1b8178223eaa88c4863ba04933d5751797b42da2076402c3dcb6b41b6f"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Prove the first crossing has the exact threshold value",
          "text": "For finite τ=q, the crossing event gives e≤Λ(q). If Λ(q)>e, continuity on [0,q], Λ(0)=0 and e≥0 yield s≤q with Λ(s)=e by the intermediate value theorem. Strictness forces s<q, while the crossing equivalence forces q≤s, a contradiction. At time zero the same event proves e>0⇒τ>0 and τ(0)=0.",
          "formula": "\\tau_z(e)<\\infty\\Longrightarrow\\Lambda_z(\\tau_z(e))=e,\\qquad e>0\\Longrightarrow\\tau_z(e)>0,\\qquad\\tau_z(0)=0.",
          "lean": "  have hfinite (y xRef : E) (z : E × E) (e : ℝ≥0)\n      (hn : τ y xRef z e ≠ ⊤) :\n      Λ y xRef z (τ y xRef z e).untopA = (e : ℝ) := by\n    let q : ℝ≥0 := (τ y xRef z e).untop hn\n    have hq : (q : WithTop ℝ≥0) = τ y xRef z e := WithTop.coe_untop _ _\n    have hge : (e : ℝ) ≤ Λ y xRef z q :=\n      (hτle y xRef z e q).1 hq.symm.le\n    have hval : Λ y xRef z q = (e : ℝ) := by\n      apply le_antisymm _ hge\n      by_contra h\n      have hstrict : (e : ℝ) < Λ y xRef z q := not_le.mp h\n      obtain ⟨s, hs, hse⟩ := intermediate_value_Icc (show (0 : ℝ≥0) ≤ q from bot_le)\n        (hcont y xRef z).continuousOn\n        (show (e : ℝ) ∈ Set.Icc (Λ y xRef z 0) (Λ y xRef z q) from\n          ⟨by simpa only [(hbasic y xRef z).1] using e.coe_nonneg, hge⟩)\n      have hsq : s < q := by\n        by_contra hnot\n        have heq : q = s := le_antisymm (not_lt.mp hnot) hs.2\n        have hbad : Λ y xRef z q = (e : ℝ) := by simpa only [heq] using hse\n        linarith\n      have hqs : q ≤ s := by\n        exact_mod_cast hq.le.trans ((hτle y xRef z e s).2 hse.ge)\n      exact not_le_of_gt hsq hqs\n    simpa only [WithTop.untopA_eq_untop hn] using hval\n  have hpositive (y xRef : E) (z : E × E) (e : ℝ≥0) (he : 0 < e) :\n      (0 : WithTop ℝ≥0) < τ y xRef z e := by\n    apply lt_of_not_ge\n    intro h\n    have hh : (e : ℝ) ≤ 0 := by\n      simpa only [(hbasic y xRef z).1] using (hτle y xRef z e 0).1 h\n    exact not_le_of_gt (show (0 : ℝ) < e from he) hh\n  have hzero (y xRef : E) (z : E × E) : τ y xRef z 0 = 0 := by\n    apply le_antisymm _ bot_le\n    exact (hτle y xRef z 0 0).2 (by\n      simpa only [NNReal.coe_zero, (hbasic y xRef z).1] using (le_refl (0 : ℝ)))\n",
          "detail": "Exact contiguous compiled BODY; the literal local definitions and preceding facts remain in scope. The first three blocks are the internal primitive helper, then the public first-clock proof.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/ActualHazardClock.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "fd93d01583eec206285573c1f1631b94739f95471c50e1ff940e66080238e23d",
            "start_line": 292,
            "end_line": 326,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "58184e54b64c5cf72ddeea9cd6779b69edb66c66cb92ecadf84582c6deea4ebe"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Prove the first clock is jointly Borel",
          "text": "The target extended time is generated by closed lower intervals. The preimage of Iic(∞) is the whole space. For finite t, the crossing event identifies the preimage as {e≤Λ_z(t)}, a Borel inequality between the threshold coordinate and the jointly Borel cumulative hazard. This proves joint measurability, including infinite waiting.",
          "formula": "\\{(y,x_{\\rm ref},z,e):\\tau_z(e)\\le t\\}=\\{(y,x_{\\rm ref},z,e):e\\le\\Lambda_z(t)\\}\\text{ is Borel}.",
          "lean": "  have hτmeas : Measurable (fun a : (E × E) × (E × E) × ℝ≥0 =>\n      τ a.1.1 a.1.2 a.2.1 a.2.2) := by\n    apply measurable_of_Iic\n    intro b\n    induction b using WithTop.recTopCoe with\n    | top => simpa using MeasurableSet.univ\n    | coe t =>\n      have hevent : (fun a : (E × E) × (E × E) × ℝ≥0 =>\n          τ a.1.1 a.1.2 a.2.1 a.2.2) ⁻¹' Set.Iic (t : WithTop ℝ≥0) =\n          {a | (a.2.2 : ℝ) ≤ Λ a.1.1 a.1.2 a.2.1 t} := by\n        ext a\n        exact hτle a.1.1 a.1.2 a.2.1 a.2.2 t\n      rw [hevent]\n      exact measurableSet_le (measurable_coe_nnreal_real.comp measurable_snd.snd)\n        (hΛmeas.comp ((measurable_fst.prodMk measurable_snd.fst).prodMk measurable_const))\n",
          "detail": "Exact contiguous compiled BODY; the literal local definitions and preceding facts remain in scope. The first three blocks are the internal primitive helper, then the public first-clock proof.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/ActualHazardClock.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "fd93d01583eec206285573c1f1631b94739f95471c50e1ff940e66080238e23d",
            "start_line": 327,
            "end_line": 341,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "4ac98511f72e8f95ffe548722a96cb28275a6a011734b43dbef3b6cb8cf221ea"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Push forward the actual unit exponential law",
          "text": "The unit-rate exponential measure is a probability measure. Its map e↦τ_z(toNNReal e) is measurable by composing the jointly Borel clock with fixed parameters and the measurable nonnegative-part map. Hence its pushforward W_z is a probability measure. The finite-time event and Λ_z(t)≥0 identify the strict survival preimage exactly with {e>Λ_z(t)} on ℝ.",
          "formula": "W_z\\text{ is a probability measure},\\qquad\\{e:t<\\tau_z(\\max\\{e,0\\})\\}=\\{e:\\Lambda_z(t)<e\\}.",
          "lean": "  have hlaw (y xRef : E) (z : E × E) : IsProbabilityMeasure (W y xRef z) ∧\n      ∀ t : ℝ≥0, (W y xRef z).real (Set.Ioi (t : WithTop ℝ≥0)) =\n        Real.exp (-Λ y xRef z t) := by\n    letI : IsProbabilityMeasure (ProbabilityTheory.expMeasure (1 : ℝ)) :=\n      ProbabilityTheory.isProbabilityMeasure_expMeasure zero_lt_one\n    have hi : Measurable (fun e : ℝ => ((y, xRef), z, Real.toNNReal e)) :=\n      measurable_const.prodMk (measurable_const.prodMk measurable_real_toNNReal)\n    have ht0 := hτmeas.comp hi\n    have ht : Measurable (fun e : ℝ => τ y xRef z (Real.toNNReal e)) := ht0\n    refine ⟨Measure.isProbabilityMeasure_map ht.aemeasurable, ?_⟩\n    intro t\n    have hpre : (fun e : ℝ => τ y xRef z (Real.toNNReal e)) ⁻¹'\n        Set.Ioi (t : WithTop ℝ≥0) = Set.Ioi (Λ y xRef z t) := by\n      ext e\n      change (t : WithTop ℝ≥0) < τ y xRef z (Real.toNNReal e) ↔ Λ y xRef z t < e\n      rw [← not_le, hτle, not_le]\n      simp only [Real.coe_toNNReal', lt_max_iff,\n        not_lt.mpr ((hbasic y xRef z).2.1 t), or_false]\n",
          "detail": "Exact contiguous compiled BODY; the literal local definitions and preceding facts remain in scope. The first three blocks are the internal primitive helper, then the public first-clock proof.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/ActualHazardClock.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "fd93d01583eec206285573c1f1631b94739f95471c50e1ff940e66080238e23d",
            "start_line": 342,
            "end_line": 359,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "078e0487a7414845cca8ad06ff0675c34dd54d1d398a6fb0c67ec53dd970efbf"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Evaluate the strict survival probability",
          "text": "Apply the measurable pushforward formula to Ioi(t). The preimage from the preceding block is Ioi(Λ_z(t)). Take the complement of Iic and use the exact Exp(1) CDF, 1−exp(−u) for u≥0, obtaining exp(−Λ_z(t)). Possible mass at infinite waiting is retained by the interval (t,∞].",
          "formula": "W_z((t,\\infty])=\\Pr\\{E>\\Lambda_z(t)\\}=1-(1-e^{-\\Lambda_z(t)})=e^{-\\Lambda_z(t)}.",
          "lean": "    change ((ProbabilityTheory.expMeasure (1 : ℝ)).map\n      (fun e : ℝ => τ y xRef z (Real.toNNReal e))\n      (Set.Ioi (t : WithTop ℝ≥0))).toReal = _\n    rw [Measure.map_apply ht measurableSet_Ioi, hpre]\n    change (ProbabilityTheory.expMeasure (1 : ℝ)).real (Set.Ioi (Λ y xRef z t)) = _\n    rw [← Set.compl_Iic, measureReal_compl measurableSet_Iic, probReal_univ,\n      ← ProbabilityTheory.cdf_eq_real, ProbabilityTheory.cdf_expMeasure_eq zero_lt_one]\n    simp only [if_pos ((hbasic y xRef z).2.1 t), one_mul]\n    ring\n",
          "detail": "Exact contiguous compiled BODY; the literal local definitions and preceding facts remain in scope. The first three blocks are the internal primitive helper, then the public first-clock proof.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/ActualHazardClock.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "fd93d01583eec206285573c1f1631b94739f95471c50e1ff940e66080238e23d",
            "start_line": 360,
            "end_line": 368,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "9671823203625aa16a81262410b8f9c594ad0789cfa84e00a14aae1614cdd088"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Extract the extended waiting lower bound and zero-cap branch",
          "text": "If C(z)>0 and τ is finite, the exact threshold identity and integrated cap give e=Λ_z(τ)≤C(z)τ, so e/C(z)≤τ. If τ=∞ the extended inequality is automatic. If C(z)=0 and e>0, every Λ_z(t)≤0<e; the no-hit equivalence gives τ=∞. Collect all ten conclusion groups, preserving the finite-hit guards.",
          "formula": "C(z)>0\\Longrightarrow\\tau_z(e)\\ge e/C(z),\\qquad C(z)=0,\\ e>0\\Longrightarrow\\tau_z(e)=\\infty.",
          "lean": "  have hwait (y xRef : E) (z : E × E) (e : ℝ≥0) :\n      (0 < C y xRef z →\n        (Real.toNNReal ((e : ℝ) / C y xRef z) : WithTop ℝ≥0) ≤ τ y xRef z e) ∧\n      (C y xRef z = 0 → 0 < e → τ y xRef z e = ⊤) := by\n    constructor\n    · intro hC\n      by_cases hn : τ y xRef z e = ⊤\n      · simp only [hn, le_top]\n      · let q : ℝ≥0 := (τ y xRef z e).untop hn\n        have hq : (q : WithTop ℝ≥0) = τ y xRef z e := WithTop.coe_untop _ _\n        have hval : Λ y xRef z q = (e : ℝ) := by\n          simpa only [WithTop.untopA_eq_untop hn] using hfinite y xRef z e hn\n        have hb : (e : ℝ) ≤ C y xRef z * (q : ℝ) :=\n          hval ▸ (hcaps y xRef z).2 q\n        have hdiv : (e : ℝ) / C y xRef z ≤ (q : ℝ) :=\n          (div_le_iff₀ hC).2 (by simpa only [mul_comm] using hb)\n        exact (WithTop.coe_le_coe.mpr (Real.toNNReal_le_iff_le_coe.mpr hdiv)).trans_eq hq\n    · intro hC he\n      apply (hτtop y xRef z e).2\n      intro t\n      have hb : Λ y xRef z t ≤ 0 := by simpa only [hC, zero_mul] using (hcaps y xRef z).2 t\n      exact hb.trans_lt (show (0 : ℝ) < e from he)\n  exact ⟨hΛ, hΛmeas, hInt, hbasic, hτle,\n    fun y xRef z e => ⟨hτtop y xRef z e, hfinite y xRef z e,\n      hpositive y xRef z e, hzero y xRef z⟩, hτmeas, hlaw, hcaps, hwait⟩\n",
          "detail": "Exact contiguous compiled BODY; the literal local definitions and preceding facts remain in scope. The first three blocks are the internal primitive helper, then the public first-clock proof.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/ActualHazardClock.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "fd93d01583eec206285573c1f1631b94739f95471c50e1ff940e66080238e23d",
