      "lean_statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space, including rank zero. Let V:E→ℝ be C², let α,β≥0 satisfy 0<α≤β and α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for all x,v, and let η>0 with βη≤1. For arbitrary y,xRef and z=(x,p), define c=y−η∇V(xRef), Φ_t(z)=(c+cos(t)(x−c)+√η sin(t)p, −sin(t)(x−c)/√η+cos(t)p), λ(xRef,(u,q))=√η max(0,⟨q,∇V(u)−∇V(xRef)⟩), H(z)=(η⁻¹‖x−c‖²+‖p‖²)/2, and C(z)=√η β√(2H(z))(√(2ηH(z))+‖c−xRef‖). For t≥0 put Λ_z(t)=∫₀ᵗλ(xRef,Φ_s(z))ds and τ_z(e)=inf{t≥0:Λ_z(t)≥e}, returning ∞ when this set is empty. Let W_z be the pushforward of Exp(1) on ℝ by e↦τ_z(max(e,0)). Then: (1) Λ is jointly continuous in y,xRef,z,t; (2) Λ is jointly Borel; (3) the actual orbit rate is integrable on every finite [0,t]; (4) Λ_z(0)=0, Λ_z(t)≥0 and Λ_z is nondecreasing; (5) for every e,t≥0, τ_z(e)≤t iff e≤Λ_z(t); (6) τ_z(e)=∞ iff Λ_z(t)<e for every finite t, finite τ_z(e) satisfies Λ_z(τ_z(e))=e, e>0 implies τ_z(e)>0, and τ_z(0)=0; (7) τ is jointly Borel in y,xRef,z,e; (8) W_z is a probability measure on [0,∞] and W_z((t,∞])=exp(−Λ_z(t)) for every finite t; (9) C(z)≥0 and Λ_z(t)≤C(z)t; (10) C(z)>0 implies max(e/C(z),0)≤τ_z(e), while C(z)=0 and e>0 imply τ_z(e)=∞. Every conclusion is derived for the actual flow and rate using their compiled laws. No unbounded-hazard or almost-sure finite-wait assumption is made. This is one flow-segment clock law used by AppendixA.1(A.1) and the future recursion(A.2). Recursive paths, nonexplosion, Markov memorylessness, invariance, terminal sampling kernels, main bounds and query costs remain open.",
