        "lean": "E is a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its compatible norm and Borel measurable structure; product spaces use product structures. Rank zero is allowed. V:E→ℝ is C² on all E. The nonnegative α,β satisfy 0<α and α≤β, and α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v∈E. η is real, η>0 and βη≤1. These are exactly the six original analytic callers. Flow/rate continuity, integrability, hazard monotonicity, an arbitrary cap, positivity of energy and finiteness of a random wait are never supplied as callers."
